  actual: '<div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Map workspace</span><h2>Layers and legend</h2><p>Only integrated scientific layers will appear as available map controls.</p></div><section aria-label="Elevation" data-scientific-category="Elevation"><h3>Elevation</h3><p class="supporting">Terrain height relative to the source vertical reference; posting does not establish effective resolution or absolute accuracy.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Hillshade" data-scientific-category="Hillshade"><h3>Hillshade</h3><p class="supporting">Artificial illumination reveals terrain shape. Intensity is unitless and does not represent actual sunlight or terrain safety.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Slope" data-scientific-category="Slope"><h3>Slope</h3><p class="supporting">Local terrain gradient in degrees. Display classes are not astronaut safety thresholds or a traversability assessment.</p><div class="data-product"><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox" checked=""/>Slope<span class="badge cyan">Derived</span></label><p class="supporting">Availability: available</p><label class="field-label" for="opacity-jezero-slope">Slope opacity <span class="mono">60%</span></label><input id="opacity-jezero-slope" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="60"/><div class="legend-detail"><strong>Slope (display-derived, degrees) (deg)</strong><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#264653;width:16px;height:12px"></span>0</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#2a9d8f;width:16px;height:12px"></span>3.5</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#e9c46a;width:16px;height:12px"></span>8.75</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#f4a261;width:16px;height:12px"></span>17.5</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#e76f51;width:16px;height:12px"></span>26.25</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#9d2a26;width:16px;height:12px"></span>35 and above (color saturated)</p></div></div><p class="supporting">USGS Astrogeology Science Center · NASA/MRO HiRISE · derived from the Mars 2020 TRN DTM mosaic (DOI 10.5066/P9REJ9JN) · Derived display measurement, not a hazard or trafficability product: slope = atan(sqrt((dz/dx)^2 + (dz/dy)^2)) computed by team/jezero/terrain/build_slope.mjs on the display pixel grid from bilinearly sampled DTM elevations, with Mars ground spacing (r = 3,396,190 m). The measurement baseline is therefore the display pixel size, not the native 1 m post: ~10 m at z14, ~19 m at z13, ~150 m at z10 and ~5 km at z5, so low zooms show a smoothed regional gradient and the same terrain reads slightly gentler as zoom decreases. Slope alone says nothing about bearing strength, rock abundance, sand trapping or rover trafficability; unknown terrain is not safe terrain. Vertical-datum caveats and the far-west CR stereo bias (~3-5 m) documented for the Elevation layer apply to the underlying elevations; the display shares the region display-transform caveats (planetocentric display latitude on Web Mercator).</p><p class="supporting">Coverage: Slope derived from the same USGS Mars 2020 TRN HiRISE DTM mosaic (JEZ_hirise_soc_006, 1 m/px, DOI 10.5066/P9REJ9JN): display tiles cover 77.2229-77.4931 E, 18.4020-18.5197 N (Web-Mercator XYZ, zooms 5-14, 193 RGBA tiles; tile ranges span the region extent, data only within the footprint). Pixels outside the DTM footprint - including the west margin 77.1868-77.2229 E - are transparent (no terrain data there).</p><details><summary>Scientific processing and verification</summary><p class="supporting">Slope measures local terrain steepness in degrees. Higher values indicate steeper terrain, but slope alone does not determine astronaut traversability.</p><dl class="metadata"><div><dt>Source verification</dt><dd>VERIFIED</dd></div><div><dt>Processing verification</dt><dd>UNVERIFIED</dd></div><div><dt>Independent registration</dt><dd>UNVERIFIED</dd></div><div><dt>Nominal source posting</dt><dd>1 m; not effective resolution</dd></div><div><dt>Valid-data mask</dt><dd>Legacy alpha retained; invalid cardinal neighbors replaced with center elevation by legacy generator, potentially flattening edges.</dd></div></dl><p class="supporting">Display-dependent central differences, ~4.825m at z14 / ~9.65m at z13 / ~2470m at z5 at 18.46N. Existing source indexing lacks pixel-center -0.5. No numeric changes; color saturates at 35deg while sampled slopes reach 54.4deg.</p></details><details><summary>Source and processing details</summary><a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/P9REJ9JN" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">USGS Mars 2020 Terrain Relative Navigation HiRISE DTM mosaic (1 m/px)</a><p class="supporting">Product verified via its DOI landing page, FGDC metadata XML and ISIS label before download; source index https://asc-pds-services.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/mosaic/mars2020_trn/HiRISE/index.html.</p><p class="supporting">Four-layer audit: standalone hillshade uses team/jezero/terrain/build_hillshade.py from the numeric source, artificial azimuth 315 / elevation 45 degrees, native pixel centers and Mars ground spacing, strict nodata support. Source SHA256, exact extrema, native mask geometry and per-tile hashes are in team/jezero/terrain/hillshade_report.json. Native label longitude domain is 180; positive Jezero longitudes are unchanged in application 0-360 east convention.</p><p class="supporting">Uncompressed 32-bit float GeoTIFF, 21,400 x 21,488, 1 m/px, equirectangular (latTs0/lon0), planetocentric latitude, east-positive, D_Mars_2000_Sphere r=3,396,190 m; ISIS label UpperLeftCornerX/Y = 4577366.0/1106618.0 m; GDAL nodata tag -3.4028e+38; label footprint 77.2229-77.5840 E, 18.3068-18.6693 N (reproduced exactly by the GeoTIFF georeferencing tags).</p><p class="supporting">Audit (team/jezero/terrain/audit_terrain.mjs, report team/jezero/terrain/audit_report.json): structure, georeferencing, nodata and value-range checks pass; PLACES cross-check over 30,445 traverse points: median DTM-PLACES +0.025 m, RMS 1.6 m, abs P95 4.3 m - the areoid-relative vertical datum is verified empirically.</p><p class="supporting">FGDC published value range (-2659.8 to -1942.1 m) is understated: sampled values reach -1639.971 m in a contiguous western-rim band (lon 77.25-77.29 E). Confirmed real terrain by rover ground truth (PLACES sol 1354: -1786.0 m at 18.4575 N, 77.2685 E; DTM matched within ~5 m) - recorded as a documented metadata caveat, not a data defect.</p><p class="supporting">USGS documents uncompensated y-parallax in the Jezero_CR stereo components of this mosaic; the traverse bins crossing that area show a small positive bias (~+3 m mean, abs P95 ~4.9 m) consistent with the USGS quality warning.</p><p class="supporting">Display tiles /maps/jezero/terrain-tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}.png derived by team/jezero/terrain/build_terrain.mjs: 193 256 px Web-Mercator XYZ RGBA tiles, zooms 5-14, shaded hypsometric elevation (p2-p98 ramp -2620/-1770 m) x analytic hillshade (sun 315 deg az / 45 deg alt); bilinear sampling; nodata transparent; the large source raster stays in local storage (team/jezero/terrain/, gitignored) and is never committed.</p><p class="supporting">Public domain USGS release; cite the product authors via the DOI.</p><p class="supporting">Four-layer audit identified incorrect Earth-sized gradient spacing and flat-ground illumination in the legacy elevation tint; existing pixels retained with processing UNVERIFIED. Legacy slope/elevation sampling also omits half-post center correction. These display issues do not invalidate the source elevations; standalone hillshade does not reuse those calculations. Independent absolute horizontal registration remains UNVERIFIED; historical PLACES height agreement is not independent positional control.</p><p class="supporting">Display tiles are derived, resampled and hillshaded - not the native 1 m posts; not a route-safety or engineering product.</p><p class="supporting">The far-west CR stereo component retains a small (~3-5 m) vertical bias per USGS quality notes; values there are display-grade only.</p></details></div></section><section aria-label="Thermal" data-scientific-category="Thermal"><h3>Thermal</h3><p class="supporting">Qualitative infrared mosaic brightness. This display is not calibrated temperature or thermal inertia; observation context differs by source.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Basemaps"><h3>Basemaps</h3><p class="supporting">Optical context and mission imagery.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Map overlays"><h3>Map overlays</h3><p class="supporting">Recorded traverses and dataset coverage outlines; these do not establish waypoint eligibility.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><h3>Interface preview</h3><p class="supporting">Demonstration controls below affect schematic artwork only.</p><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/>Show schematic preview <span class="badge science">Scenario</span></label><button class="full">View scientific data register</button>'
